course: dictionary
lesson: 10552
title: Unbalance and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To unbalance something is to make it lose its balance, so it tips or wobbles. Put a heavy bag on one end of a seesaw and it tips down: the bag has unbalanced the seesaw. The word also describes fairness. When one team has many more good players, the game is no longer even.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning that fits. «When one force is bigger, the forces are unbalanced and the object speeds up, slows down or changes direction.» Here unbalanced is an adjective. The clue is "one force is bigger": the forces are not equal, so the object moves. Ask yourself what the sentence would say if things were even.
explain: Unbalance can also mean to upset a person so much that they cannot think clearly, but that is an older use you will mostly find in old books. The usual word for a lack of balance is imbalance. If you are unsure, try imbalance in the sentence: if it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Unbalance is a verb: to unbalance something is to make it lose its balance.
fact: «Unbalanced» is the adjective, as in «an unbalanced diet», which has too much of one kind of food and not enough of others.
fact: «When one force is bigger, the forces are unbalanced and the object speeds up, slows down or changes direction.»
fact: In maths, an equation is like a balance, so adding to one side only unbalances it.
fact: Unbalance as a noun is rare; imbalance is the word people normally use for a lack of balance.
exercise: «When one force is bigger, the forces are unbalanced.» What does unbalanced mean here? | *Not equal, so the object moves | Perfectly equal, so the object stays still | Painted in bright colours | Very heavy and slow
exercise: Ben says a team with many more good players will unbalance the game. What does unbalance mean in this sentence? | Makes the game quieter | *Makes it unfair or uneven | Makes the game longer | Makes the ball lose its shape
exercise: Which word is the usual name for a lack of balance? | *Imbalance | Rebalance | Balloon | Balancing
test: Adding a heavy bag to one end of a seesaw will do what? | Make it quieter | Make it stay perfectly level | *Unbalance it so it tips down | Make the seesaw disappear
test: Which best describes an unbalanced game? | *Uneven, with one team much stronger | Quiet and calm | Short and fast | Even, with both teams equally good
exam: Ruby reads «The unfair rules unbalanced the contest.» What does unbalanced most likely mean? | Made the contest into a dance | Made the contest end early | Made the contest sunny and warm | *Made the contest uneven and unfair
